1. the hierarchy, up to BaseException
   Exception            Exception < BaseException
   RuntimeError         RuntimeError < Exception < BaseException
   ValueError           ValueError < Exception < BaseException
   TypeError            TypeError < Exception < BaseException
   NameError            NameError < Exception < BaseException
   AttributeError       AttributeError < Exception < BaseException
   ZeroDivisionError    ZeroDivisionError < ArithmeticError < Exception < BaseException
   KeyError             KeyError < LookupError < Exception < BaseException
   StopIteration        StopIteration < Exception < BaseException
   IndexError           IndexError < LookupError < Exception < BaseException
   OSError              OSError < Exception < BaseException
   FileNotFoundError    FileNotFoundError < OSError < Exception < BaseException
   RecursionError       RecursionError < RuntimeError < Exception < BaseException
   NotImplementedError  NotImplementedError < RuntimeError < Exception < BaseException
   ModuleNotFoundError  ModuleNotFoundError < ImportError < Exception < BaseException
   SyntaxError          SyntaxError < Exception < BaseException
   SystemExit           SystemExit < BaseException
   KeyboardInterrupt    KeyboardInterrupt < BaseException
   MemoryError          MemoryError < Exception < BaseException
2. what except Exception catches (except Exception inside, except BaseException outside)
   RuntimeError         caught by except Exception
   ValueError           caught by except Exception
   StopIteration        caught by except Exception
   FileNotFoundError    caught by except Exception
   SystemExit           SLIPPED PAST it; except BaseException caught SystemExit
   KeyboardInterrupt    SLIPPED PAST it; except BaseException caught KeyboardInterrupt
   MemoryError          caught by except Exception
   NotImplementedError  caught by except Exception
   ModuleNotFoundError  caught by except Exception
   RecursionError       caught by except Exception
3. a bare except is except BaseException -- the opposite default
   bare except caught SystemExit; isinstance(e, Exception): False
   isinstance(Exception(), BaseException)  True
   Exception.__mro__[1].__name__           BaseException
4. a bare except swallows sys.exit (the anti-pattern)
   swallowed SystemExit (code 1); the program goes on
5. a real stack overflow IS an Exception here
   except Exception caught RecursionError
6. NotImplementedError is a RuntimeError, so except Exception catches it
   except Exception caught NotImplementedError
